------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- POST-ARCHAEOLOGY BIDI ROADMAP
--
-- RSA correction:
--   the generic Lean theorem source remains the preferred theorem compressor,
--   but the pinned import surface required correction and the actual RSA family
--   still needs one common module plus per-context linear-map bindings before a
--   zero joint-kernel receipt can instantiate joint injectivity.
--
-- RH correction:
--   the retained Aristotle aggregate is not the historical RH owner, but it
--   preserves a content-addressed pointer to the original source archive.  The
--   archive therefore dominates a speculative reproof until recovery has been
--   attempted and its contents searched.
--
-- The production RSA authenticity route and the existing Agda/Python RH ascent
-- remain unchanged and orthogonal to these proof/source-recovery probes.
------------------------------------------------------------------------

